{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "2d98d74e-5102-8e5b-918f-5cab13e387e3",
  "created_at": "2025-12-04T11:47:30-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Sal DeLuca",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Greg Lombardi",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:42:07-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Greg."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:42:10-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, hi Greg. Sal DeLuca here. I'm trying to get a curb cut put in for my driveway and I've been bounced around already. Somebody told me it's you, somebody else told me it's Public Services."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:42:26-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, yeah, that happens a lot. Let me get the basics. What's the address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:42:33-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "248 Dixon Street. North End, off Broadway kind of, back toward the water side."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:42:40-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. And right now there's no driveway there at all? Just the curb?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:42:47-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, full curb, nothing. I park on the street and it's a circus. I want a single-car cut, nothing crazy. Just so I can pull in off the road."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:43:00-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. So a driveway curb cut is its own permit. It goes through the city, and Public Services has a say on the curb and the sidewalk part, since that's city property. We handle the zoning side, whether the driveway itself is allowed on your lot."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:43:20-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So two offices. Great. Who do I hire for it? Do I just call a paving guy, or is there some list?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:43:30-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No list that I'd hand you. You'd want a licensed contractor who does curb and driveway work, somebody who's pulled these permits in Newport before. They usually know the drill and can file it for you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:43:46-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And who actually says yes? Is it you, or the Public Services people, or what?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:43:53-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Both, in a way. Public Services approves the work in the street right-of-way. We sign off on the driveway on your property. You need both before anybody cuts a curb."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:44:06-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wonderful. Two yeses. Like asking my mother and my father."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:44:11-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[pause] Pretty much, yeah."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:44:14-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "How long does that take? Roughly. I'm not holding you to it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:44:20-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "If the application's complete and the plan is clear, you're often looking at a couple of weeks, sometimes a little more. If something's missing, that's what stretches it. And in winter, even once it's approved, your contractor may not get to the concrete until the weather loosens up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:44:41-05:00",
      "duration": 23,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, that figures. I'd like it done before spring anyway. Why the hurry, you ask? Because of the parking, honestly. My ex lives a few streets over and the kids switch houses on Wednesdays. So I'm dragging bags and backpacks from wherever I end up parking, half a block away, in the dark."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:45:04-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, I get that. Well, a driveway would help with that. What you want to bring in is a simple sketch of the lot, showing the house, where the driveway would go, and the width of the cut."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:45:21-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can draw that. Or the contractor does it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:45:26-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Contractor can do it. Often better if he does, because he'll know what the street side needs. Just make sure it shows the distance from the cut to any utility pole, tree, or hydrant out front."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:45:42-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There's a telephone pole kind of close to where I'd want it. Like, close."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:45:49-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Then that's the thing to put on the sketch. If it's too close, they may ask you to shift the opening over. Better to find out on paper than after the curb's chopped."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:46:03-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right. Do I come down there to file, or can I send it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:46:09-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You can drop it off here at the counter, or your contractor can. If you want, I'll take your number so someone can call if there's a question on the application."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:46:23-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. It's 401-555-0192."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:46:25-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "555-0192, got it. And that's the cell?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:46:29-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, the cell. I pick up unless I'm on a roof, which today I am not, so you're lucky."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:46:38-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good to know. We're open weekdays during regular hours, so come in whenever suits you and ask for zoning."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:46:47-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So, to recap, because I've been burned already today: hire a licensed guy, he does the sketch, file with you, and Public Services signs off on the street part. Two approvals, couple weeks if I'm lucky."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:47:03-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it. The application will walk you through the Public Services piece. One thing: ask your contractor whether he files both at once. It saves you a trip."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:47:15-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright, I'll ask. Thanks, Greg. At least you gave me a straight answer, which is more than the last two."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:47:24-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. Good luck with it, Sal."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-04T11:47:28-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yep. Take care."
    }
  ],
